goldenera.fi"},{"lap":0,"text":"Few drivers wore gloves and the great champion Boillot refused to even wear something on his head. He drove the Grand Prix bareheaded.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":1,"text":"The unknown Max Sailer, a cocky DMG engineer who was new in grand prix racing, went flat out, had passed no fewer than 12 of his rivals and was leading at the end of the 1st lap to the disbelief of everyone.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":31},{"lap":1,"text":"Champoiseau had smashed his Schneider against a balustrade at Rive-de-Gier but immediately carried on.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":8},{"lap":1,"text":"Salzer loses time on the opening lap; his plugs have oiled up.","q":false,"c":2},{"lap":2,"text":"When Costantini (#26 Aquila Italiana) abandoned on the 2nd lap, having broken the fuel tank, the field was down to 36 cars.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":36},{"lap":3,"text":"Sailer still held the lead, now 77 seconds ahead of Boillot while the first four positions stayed the same.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":31},{"lap":4,"text":"Boillot stopped for twenty seconds at his pits and Sailer passed the Peugeot in front of the grandstand, leading now also on the road.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":4,"text":"Sailer laps in 20m06s.","q":false,"c":31},{"lap":5,"text":"Boillot pits again: two non-slip tyres swapped for smooth ones.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":6,"text":"After having led for nearly two hours, Sailer's engine came to a stop on lap six most likely with broken connecting rods.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":31},{"lap":6,"text":"Boillot's Peugeot took the lead to the enjoyment of the French crowd.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":7,"text":"Boillot stops to change a smooth tyre; Lautenschlager runs second, just over a minute behind.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":8,"text":"Guinness (#36 Sunbeam) dropped from 6th to 14th place spending 14 minutes in the pits with engine trouble.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":22},{"lap":9,"text":"Boillot was clearly faster than everyone else, although he stopped again on the 9th lap, changed the right rear to an anti-slip, took a drink and immediately thereafter he was gone.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":10,"text":"Duray falls from 4th to 11th, losing 12 minutes with a tyre defect.","q":false,"c":7},{"lap":11,"text":"While the mechanic changed the four tires, Lautenschlager refilled fuel, oil, and water, also took time to swallow a few glasses of water mixed with champaign.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":13,"text":"Chassagne (#10 Sunbeam) in 7th place disappeared with a broken connecting rod after the 12th lap.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":17},{"lap":14,"text":"Boillot was first ahead of Wagner (#40 Mercedes) who had pushed for two laps with times below 21 minutes, helping him to pass Lautenschlager who was continuing his steady pace.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":14,"text":"Goux could brake later, and in the Death Turn he was neck and neck with the German, but was afraid to take the risk and had to slow down.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":3},{"lap":15,"text":"Wagner stopped at the pits where he and his mechanic changed the four wheels in 59 seconds.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":16,"text":"Lautenschlager began his attack on the 16th lap with a time in 21m16s, reducing the gap to Boillot from 2m28s to 2m05s.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":17,"text":"Szisz, changing a rear tyre by the roadside, is struck by Breckheimer's Opel; his shoulder is dislocated.","q":false,"c":18},{"lap":17,"text":"The difference of almost 2 minutes propelled the Mercedes to only 14 seconds behind the champion of France.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":18,"text":"Lautenschlager pushed even harder with his fastest time in 20m33s. He was now first, 33 seconds ahead of Boillot who could only pull off a lap in 21m20s.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":19,"text":"Boillot, struggling with failing brakes and uncertain steering, falls 67 seconds behind; Wagner is only seconds behind him.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":20,"text":"After 7h08m18s, Lautenschlager's white Mercedes was first to cross the finish line. Boillot on his last lap retired with a broken motor.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":20,"text":"Wagner finished second 1m36s behind and Salzer arrived almost five minutes later in third place.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1}]}